        <section id="intro" class="card">
            <h2>Introduction to Cloud Paradigms</h2>
            <p>Cloud Computing represents a monumental shift in how computational power, information networks, and application layers are distributed globally. Rather than maintaining isolated local computing engines, modern frameworks rely on virtualized resources accessible dynamically over public or private networks. Cloud security acts as a dedicated sub-discipline tasked with deploying automated guardrails, ensuring that data-driven activities comply with strict security standards.</p>
            <p>By enforcing the core pillars of the Confidentiality, Integrity, and Availability (CIA) triad, cloud architectures eliminate the limits of physical server constraints, allowing computing workloads to expand or shrink fluidly based on real-time execution demands.</p>
            
