            <h2>Pillar 1: Mathematical Foundations &amp; CIA Metrics</h2>
            <p>Information mapping requires structural calculations to guarantee system parameters remain sound against adversarial injection or transmission distortions.</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Confidentiality Mapping:</strong> Evaluated through set theory constraints where mapping function $f(u, d) \rightarrow \{0, 1\}$ strictly blocks non-authorized users.</li>
                <li><strong>Integrity Verification:</strong> Verified through cryptographic hashing sequences where the baseline target constraint operates as:
                    $$H(M) \neq H(M')$$
                </li>
                <li><strong>Availability Metrics:</strong> Quantified via deterministic mean time failures:
                    $$\text{Availability} = \frac{\text{MTBF}}{\text{MTBF} + \text{MTTR}}$$
                </li>
            </ul>
