            <h2>Pillar 3: Algorithmic Keys &amp; AES-GCM Crypto</h2>
            <p>Data protection relies on computational limits, using encryption mechanisms like the asymmetric RSA architecture built on prime-factor products ($n = p \times q$) to safeguard data transmissions.</p>
            <pre># Symmetric High-Throughput Cipher Pipeline Configuration
from cryptography.hazmat.primitives.ciphers import Cipher, algorithms, modes
import os

def generate_secure_crypto_stream(payload_bytes: bytes, cipher_key: bytes):
    iv = os.urandom(12)  # Secure 96-bit Initialization Vector
    engine = Cipher(algorithms.AES(cipher_key), modes.GCM(iv))
    stream_worker = engine.encryptor()
    ciphertext = stream_worker.update(payload_bytes) + stream_worker.finalize()
    return (ciphertext, iv, stream_worker.tag)
            </pre>
