        <section id="cloud-core" class="card">
            <h2>Cloud Computing Systems &amp; Virtualization Stack</h2>
            <p><strong>Cloud Computing</strong> is the on-demand, network-accessible deployment of virtualized hardware components, processing nodes, memory blocks, and database architectures over internet channels. Instead of deploying and maintaining physical systems locally, resources are leased from massive cloud provider datacenters via automated software APIs.</p>
            <p>The entire system relies on deep hardware abstraction, using hypervisors to split physical host machines into independent, multi-tenant virtual execution environments.</p>
