        <section id="service-models" class="card">
            <h2>Cloud Service Blueprints (IaaS, PaaS, SaaS Kernels)</h2>
            <p>Cloud service options are systematically categorized into three clean architecture frameworks based on the level of technical control they provide:</p>
            
            <h3>Infrastructure as a Service (IaaS)</h3>
            <p>Delivers direct, un-provisioned access to virtual machines, network configurations, and storage volumes. Administrators have full control over operating system kernels, configurations, and installed applications.</p>
            
            <h3>Platform as a Service (PaaS)</h3>
            <p>Provides pre-configured runtime stacks, application frameworks, and automated deployment hosting. Software engineers can deploy application source code directly without managing the underlying server operating systems.</p>
            
            <h3>Software as a Service (SaaS)</h3>
            <p>Delivers fully functional end-user software applications over web runtimes. The cloud provider retains entire ownership of code bases, data storage, and the underlying hosting infrastructure.</p>

