            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="shared-responsibility" class="card">
            <h2>The Shared Responsibility Model Mechanics</h2>
            <p>The Shared Responsibility Model establishes clear boundaries of operational ownership between cloud providers and clients. The hosting provider handles the baseline security <strong>of</strong> the cloud (such as physical facilities and hypervisor security), while the customer remains fully responsible for securing the data <strong>in</strong> the cloud (including encryption settings and identity configurations).</p>
            <div class="example-box">
                <strong>Core Breakdown:</strong> If a database bucket is misconfigured with public read permissions, the responsibility falls entirely on the client, as the cloud provider only maintains the underlying availability of the storage service itself.
            </div>
