        </section>

        <section id="storage-topologies" class="card">
            <h2>Distributed Object, Block &amp; File Storage Layers</h2>
            <p>Cloud data storage utilizes specialized structures tailored to specific application access patterns:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Object Storage:</strong> Flat data repositories that store files along with customizable metadata tags, accessible via web service REST APIs (e.g., AWS S3).</li>
                <li><strong>Block Storage:</strong> High-performance raw data blocks that attach directly to virtual servers, acting like local physical hard drives to support heavy transactional systems.</li>
                <li><strong>File Storage:</strong> Shared file systems accessible simultaneously across multiple server nodes using standard network protocols like NFS or SMB.</li>
            </ul>
