        <section id="containerization" class="card">
            <h2>Container Systems: Docker Engines &amp; Kubernetes</h2>
            <p>Modern applications favor lightweight container setups over traditional virtual machines. By sharing the underlying host operating system kernel, containers provide rapid boot times and consistent deployment across development and production environments.</p>
            <p>Docker standardizes the packaging of these immutable application layers, while orchestration frameworks like Kubernetes automate container deployment, horizontal scaling, and self-healing cluster recovery at scale.</p>
            <pre># Sample Deployment Manifest Architecture
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: dynamic-core-app
spec:
  replicas: 4
  template:
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: production-worker
        image: custom-registry.internal/worker:v1.0
            </pre>
